Machine-learning models (downloaded at first run, not redistributed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

With one exception (the Silero VAD model, which is compiled into the
binary — see voice_activity_detector above), Folio does not bundle model
weights in the .dmg or the Homebrew cask. The following pre-trained models
are fetched on demand from the URLs below into the user's
application-support directory the first time a feature that needs them is
used. When Privacy Mode / air-gap is on, these downloads are blocked by the
egress guard like any other request.

- Whisper GGML weights (MIT) — © OpenAI; speech-to-text. Distributed
  by the whisper.cpp project on Hugging Face.
  https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
- pyannote segmentation-3.0 (MIT, gated) — speaker-segmentation model
  by Hervé Bredin. Access is gated on Hugging Face; review the upstream
  model card before commercial deployment. Folio downloads the ONNX
  export re-hosted by the sherpa-onnx project.
  https://huggingface.co/csukuangfj/sherpa-onnx-pyannote-segmentation-3-0
  Upstream: https://huggingface.co/pyannote/segmentation-3.0
- WeSpeaker voxceleb resnet34-LM speaker embedding — the WeSpeaker
  project is Apache-2.0; the wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM checkpoint
  is published by pyannote under CC-BY-4.0. Cite: Wang et al.,
  "WeSpeaker: A Research and Production Oriented Speaker Embedding
  Learning Toolkit", ICASSP 2023.
  Upstream: https://huggingface.co/pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM

The Whisper weights come from Hugging Face; the WeSpeaker embedding model
is downloaded from the k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx GitHub releases. (The Silero VAD
model is not downloaded — it ships compiled into the binary; see
voice_activity_detector above.)

Commercial redistributors who choose to bundle any of these weights
(rather than downloading them at runtime) are responsible for verifying
each model's license terms independently.

